# build output
dist/
.astro/

# dependencies
node_modules/

# environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# editors / os
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Source documents, ignored on purpose.
#
# profile.yml carries a phone number, a visa status, and compensation targets —
# a walk-away number is not something to put in a repository that might ever be
# public, or that a future employer might ever be given access to. The résumé
# PDF carries the phone number too.
#
# Everything these files contribute to the site already lives in src/content/
# and src/data/. Keep the originals locally; if you want them versioned, make
# the repository private first and then `git add -f` them deliberately.
profile.yml
*.pdf

# Agent scratch, ignored on purpose.
#
# graphify-out/ is a knowledge graph built from this repo for an assistant to
# navigate — 700 KB of derived JSON and a standalone HTML viewer. It is a
# rebuildable index of the source, not part of it, and it goes stale the moment
# the code moves. Rebuild it with /graphify rather than versioning it.
#
# The .graphify_* files are pipeline temporaries that only survive a crashed
# run, and *.stackdump is Git Bash debris on Windows.
graphify-out/
.graphify_*
*.stackdump

# /brag output, ignored on purpose.
#
# brag-output/ is a launch video built from this repo — the rendered MP4 and its
# poster, plus the Hyperframes project that produced them. Nearly 6 MB of it is
# vendored third-party weight the site itself never loads: a music bed, a
# handful of CC0 sound effects, GSAP, and woff2 copies of the two fonts the site
# already pulls from Google.
#
# Every frame of it is derived from src/content/ and src/styles/theme.css, so it
# goes stale the moment the copy or the palette moves. Rebuild it with /brag
# rather than versioning it, and upload the MP4 wherever it is being posted.
brag-output/
brag-output-*/
